cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "pnp-general: machine-checked mathematics across fields"
authors:
  - name: "Addison"
repository-code: "https://github.com/addison-jpg/pnp-general"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
type: software
abstract: >-
  A public repository of results on Boolean circuit size with limited NOT
  gates, stated and checked in Lean 4. It includes NOT-gate lower bounds for
  OR systems (tight for disjoint sets and chains), Lean formalizations of
  known results from quantum computing and quantum gravity (the Knill gate
  count for two-qubit circuits via the KAK decomposition, the three-qubit
  CKW inequality, and PSPACE contained in P_CTC contained in EXP), and a
  computed counterexample (AG(2,8)) to the point lemma for general set
  families. Each result is labelled by how it was checked. The Lean project
  under lean/ has not yet had a full axiom audit. The repository also ships
  the asteroid (.ath) claim language and its checker. It does not claim any
  result on P versus NP.
keywords:
  - lean4
  - circuit-complexity
  - formal-verification
